  "id": "complex-ideas",
  "term": "complex ideas",
  "definition": "In associationist psychology, complex ideas are mental contents formed when many simple ideas become linked through repeated association and combine into a single whole. When the combination is extensive, the resulting idea may no longer seem obviously related to its simpler components.",
